**Target Audience

**Primary Audience

The primary audience is Jobcentre customers who would benefit from work experience, employability support and additional preparation before entering or returning to employment.

**This may include:

*Young people looking to begin their careers
*People with limited or no previous work experience
*People who have been unemployed for an extended period
*People who lack confidence in workplace environments
*People who need help improving their CV or applications
*People who want to practise interview skills
*People who are unsure which career or employment sector may suit them
*People who need help recognising their transferable skills
*People who would benefit from structured workplace experience
*People who need support understanding workplace expectations
*People who are interested in developing their communication, teamwork or digital skills

**Secondary Audience

The secondary audience includes Jobcentre staff and work coaches who will use the website to explain and promote the programme.

**The website should help staff:

*Introduce the programme to eligible customers
*Explain the programme structure and schedule
*Show customers the benefits of participating
*Answer common questions
*Direct customers towards registration or further support
*Promote the programme consistently

**Audience Needs

**Users will need:

*Simple and understandable language
*A clear explanation of what the programme involves
*Reassurance that support will be available
*A breakdown of the programme schedule
*Examples of the skills they may develop
*Information about how the programme could strengthen their CV
*Information about local sectors and opportunities
*Clear travel guidance
*An obvious way to register interest or ask for more information
